{"name":"Kid Gloves","hex":"#b6aeae","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kid gloves","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of kid glove"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid_gloves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kidskin","blocks":[{"text":"Kidskin or kid leather is a type of soft, thin leather that is traditionally used for gloves. It is widely used for other fashion purposes such as footwear and clothing. Kidskin is traditionally made from goatskin – more specifically, the skin of young goats, although equivalent leathers such as lambskin and chickenskin give the same effect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg/330px-Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidskin"},{"title":"Kid Gloves (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Kid Gloves is a 1929 American sound part-talkie pre-Code drama film directed by Ray Enright, and starring Conrad Nagel, Lois Wilson, Edward Earle, Edna Murphy, and Maude Turner Gordon. In addition to sequences with audible dialogue or talking sequences, the film features a synchronized musical score and sound effects along with English intertitles. According to the film review in Harrison's Reports, 75 percent of the total running time featured dialogue. The soundtrack was recorded using the Vitaphone sound-on-disc system. The film was released by Warner Bros. Pictures on March 23, 1929."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid_Gloves_(film)"},{"title":"Glove","blocks":[{"text":"A glove is a garment covering the hand, with separate sheaths or openings for each finger including the thumb. Gloves protect and comfort hands against cold or heat, damage by friction, abrasion or chemicals, and disease; or in turn to provide a guard for what a bare hand should not touch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG/330px-Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glove"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg/500px-Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg/1280px-Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg/500px-Pair_of_Infant%27s_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pair of infant's kidskin boots, 1890s. LACMA, M.54.21.4a-b","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APair_of_Infant's_Boots_LACMA_M.54.21.4a-b.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Vici_Kid_Advertisement_in_Vanity_Fair.png/500px-Vici_Kid_Advertisement_in_Vanity_Fair.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Vici_Kid_Advertisement_in_Vanity_Fair.png/500px-Vici_Kid_Advertisement_in_Vanity_Fair.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vici kid advertisement in Vanity Fair, 1924","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVici_Kid_Advertisement_in_Vanity_Fair.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Kid_Gloves_%281929%29_poster.jpg/500px-Kid_Gloves_%281929%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont